  "problem": "Successful SQL could be treated as join validation. Row multiplication, leading-zero loss and unmatched rows could go undetected. A tiny sample could report a universal match rate. Incompatible temporal/universe contexts could remain open. Machine and UI consumers could receive different compatibility. HCRIS-to-NPPES could claim CCN=NPI. R08 could be treated as complete with fewer than fifteen qualified routes. Editing sealed identity join-routes.mjs would break WP7.",
